---
import { ColumnExplorer } from './ColumnExplorer';
---

<section id="segment" class="section-spacing border-b border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--surface-tint)]">
  <div class="site-container">
    
    <!-- Introduction: 2-3 sentences per brief -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-[var(--brand)] mb-3">
        ON-DISK FILE FORMAT
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-[var(--ink)] tracking-tight mb-4">
        Look inside a segment file (.mastidb)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed prose-measure mb-6">
        In MastiDB, every column is stored on disk in two dedicated files: a 40-byte binary metadata header and a memory-mapped payload file. The payload organizes dictionary offsets, raw UTF-8 strings, fixed-width row IDs, and serialized Roaring Bitmaps into one continuous address space.
      </p>

      <!-- Short, crisp bullet points right after section paragraph per user request -->
      <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--muted)] max-w-2xl mb-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
          <span><strong class="text-[var(--ink)] font-semibold">Dual-file segment layout:</strong> A 40-byte header (<code class="font-mono text-xs bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[var(--ink)]">.meta</code>) defines ten 32-bit byte boundaries; an unpadded payload file (<code class="font-mono text-xs bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[var(--ink)]">.mastidb</code>) stores the data.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
          <span><strong class="text-[var(--ink)] font-semibold">Contiguous address space:</strong> Packs dictionary offsets, sorted UTF-8 values, encoded row IDs, and Roaring Bitmaps back-to-back with zero wasted padding.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] mt-2 shrink-0"></span>
          <span><strong class="text-[var(--ink)] font-semibold">O(1) arithmetic addressing:</strong> Fixed 4-byte integers enable row <em class="italic">i</em> lookups via direct math (<code class="font-mono text-xs bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[var(--ink)]">offset + i × 4</code>) without pointer chasing or B-Trees.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Interactive Working Component Reused from old-site, adapted to design tokens -->
    <div>
      <ColumnExplorer client:visible />
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
